# F37 stash exports: 110 MiB and 103 MiB, both over GitHub's 100 MiB hard
# limit, so tracking them makes the repository unpushable. Stripped from the
# unpushed history on 2026-07-27 (RH's call) and kept on disk. Regenerate via
# the F37 stash export path; cite as local-only artifacts in findings.
data/f37_stash_generations.jsonl
data/f37_stash_generations_scored.csv

# Superseded by parquet+zstd exports (9x smaller, same rows).
data/f20x_beams.csv
data/f20x_kinship.csv

# Machine-local seat identity for the agentdocket coordination store. Not
# tracked (RH, 2026-07-27): it names which agent seat this checkout signs as,
# which is a property of the machine, not of the code. Committing it would
# hand every clone the same identity and let two processes sign as one seat --
# the mis-signing failure the tool exists to prevent. Each checkout runs
# `docket init <seat>` for itself.
.docket-seat

# Sealed exploratory results: readable only at the holding seat until the
# corresponding design freezes. The pen has repo write access as of docket
# [467], so committing these would broadcast exactly what the seal withholds.
# The sha256 is published on the docket; the content is not.
data/sealed/

# twp JSONL transport files — canonical store is HashStash; archives in data/archive/
data/twp_cloud/
data/archive/*.tar.gz

# ── transport and redundant backups (added 2026-07-31) ────────────────────
# The cloud runner's JSONL is a TRANSPORT format, not the store: 594 MB that
# twp_ingest.py has already merged into data/raw/cache. Committing it would
# near-double a repo whose history has already had oversized blobs stripped
# once, to preserve data that exists in two other places.
data/twp_grid_v3/
data/twp_cloud/

# FILE-LEVEL BACKUPS OF VERSION-CONTROLLED FILES ARE REDUNDANT WITH GIT.
# I made three ~5 MB copies of grid_spec.json tonight before editing it --
# pre-reorder, with-falcon, pre-fastfirst -- when `git show <sha>:path` already
# holds every one of them. The named variants that a RUN depends on stay
# (grid_spec_repair*.json); the "before I edited it" copies do not.
data/*.pre-*.json
data/*-backup-*.json

# instance state, same class as the already-ignored .vastai.json
.vastai.json.*
# Per-run instance state: .vastai.m05.json and every future sibling. The two
# rules above name .vastai.json and its dotted suffixes and MISS .vastai.<run>,
# which is the form the M04/M05 runs actually write -- a pattern pinned to the
# spelling that existed when it was written. Ignore the whole family.
.vastai.*

# Cloud transport for the 32B/Falcon phases. Merged into data/raw/cache by
# twp_ingest.py; committing it would duplicate the store in git.
data/twp_phase32b/
data/twp_phasefalcon/

# ── TWP TRANSPORT PAYLOAD ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `git add -A` in this repo stages 1,701 untracked files totalling 13.40 GB and
# takes minutes doing it. This is not hypothetical: on 2026-08-09 a DOC-ONLY
# commit (four README/CAMPAIGN files) was one `add -A` away from writing the
# whole twp tree into .git, where it would have survived any revert and then
# failed the push on GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit.
#
# These directories are TRANSPORT, not the store. The canonical stash is
# LITMOD_DATA_DIR; twp_ingest.py merges these into it. Committing them
# duplicates the store in git — the same reason data/twp_phase32b/ and
# data/twp_phasefalcon/ are ignored above.
#
# MEASURED, and the scoping follows the measurement rather than the extension:
#     *.hidden.f32   190 files   8.68 GB    0 tracked anywhere -> safe globally
#     *.f16          231 files   4.32 GB    0 tracked anywhere -> safe globally
#     twp *.jsonl    231 files   0.20 GB    13 .jsonl ARE tracked elsewhere,
#                                           so this one is PATH-SCOPED, never
#                                           a bare *.jsonl
# `data/f11_twp/hidden_manifest.json` is tracked and stays tracked: it is .json,
# not .jsonl, and no rule below touches it.
*.f16
*.hidden.f32
data/f11_twp*/*.jsonl

# Derived analysis pickles. Nothing rebuilds from them that cannot rebuild from
# their producer, 0 are tracked, and meta/M02_frame_exit/results/dp.pkl is 8.8 MB
# of embeddings that pole_axis_build.py regenerates in minutes.
*.pkl

# ── Y ANALYSIS TABLES ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Derived from data/raw/y_y-*/ plus results/y_confirmatory_coded.jsonl by
# scripts/y_build_tables.py, in about 20 minutes. ~10.6M token rows, a few
# hundred MB. Rebuildable, so not committed.
#
# PATH-SCOPED, NOT `*.parquet`: 131 parquets ARE tracked in this repo and a
# bare extension rule would silently ignore every one of them. Same trap the
# twp jsonl rule above had to avoid.
meta/M01_displacement/results/y_tokens/
meta/M01_displacement/results/y_passages.parquet

# M03 plan B bulk outputs: 115 MB, DETERMINISTIC from committed producers over
# a hashed population, and larger than anything else tracked under meta/*.
# The small analysis tables they feed (b_arm_cells.csv, b_arm_by_lineage.csv,
# b_word_delta_by_word.csv) ARE tracked, so nothing quotable lives only here.
# Regenerate:
#   uv run python meta/M03_proceduralization/scripts/b_twp_institutional.py --run
#   uv run python meta/M03_proceduralization/scripts/b_word_delta.py --run
# PATH-SCOPED for the same reason as the parquet rule above.
meta/M03_proceduralization/results/b_pair_prompt.jsonl
meta/M03_proceduralization/results/b_fields.jsonl
meta/M03_proceduralization/results/b_word_delta_cells.csv.gz
meta/M03_proceduralization/results/c_cells.csv.gz
meta/M03_proceduralization/results/c_word_delta_cells.csv.gz

# M03 plan D bulk output: 57 MB, above GitHub's 50 MiB warning, DETERMINISTIC
# from a committed producer over a fixed population. The report is computed
# from it on demand (`d_ladder_fields.py --report`) and the quotable numbers
# live in the finding, so nothing is only here. Regenerate:
#   uv run python meta/M03_proceduralization/scripts/d_ladder_fields.py --run
meta/M03_proceduralization/results/d_ladder_fields.csv
meta/M03_proceduralization/results/e_field_flow_arms.parquet
.migrate_hidden/

# M06 mediation word tables: 369 MB of DERIVED per-word rows, regenerated by
# scripts/m06_mediation.py from frozen inputs in one pass. The producer and the
# collapsed results (mediation_pairs, mediation_corr_words, the JSONs) are
# committed; these are the intermediate the producer walks to build them.
# Sized here so the next reader knows what the rule is worth rather than
# guessing: 265.1 + 61.9 + 42.3 MB.
meta/M06_generation/results/mediation_words.parquet
meta/M06_generation/results/mediation_words_byprompt.parquet
meta/M06_generation/results/mediation_words_joined.parquet
